tient intake within hospital settings. Their responsibilities encompass both technical procedures and patient education, ensuring comprehensive care for individuals under their supervision.", "MÉDICOS:Médicos are doctors who assess patients' nutritional status and collaborate with the Unidad de Nutrición for dietary needs.", "RESOLUCIÓN RES AP (2003) 3:A resolution by the Council of Europe regarding food and nutritional care in hospitals, establishing recommendations for improving patient care.", "REGLAMENTO 1169/2011:A regulation in the European Union that sets legal standards for food information to consumers, including nutritional labeling in collective dining settings like hospitals.", "ISO 22000:2005:ISO 22000:2005 is an international standard that ensures food safety based on the APPCC system and is similar in structure to ISO 9000.", "GUÍA DE PRÁCTICAS CORRECTAS DE HIGIENE Y MANIPULACIÓN:A document that outlines the fundamental hygiene requirements for food operations to ensure food safety.", "ANÁLISIS MICROBIOLÓGICOS:Microbiological analyses conducted periodically on food and surfaces in hospitals to ensure safety and hygiene.", "SEGURIDAD ALIMENTARIA:Food safety practices aimed at preventing foodborne illnesses and ensuring the health of consumers, particularly in hospital settings.", "PERSONAL DE COCINA:Kitchen staff responsible for food preparation and ensuring hygiene standards are met in hospital kitchens.", "TOXIINFECCIONES ALIMENTARIAS:"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}